<title>UK: LONDON TEA AUCTION SEES STRONG GENERAL DEMAND.</title>
<headline>LONDON TEA AUCTION SEES STRONG GENERAL DEMAND.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strong general demand marked the latest auction held by the Tea Brokers' Association of London on Monday.</p>
<p>Bright and medium East Africans saw active competition and gained 5 to 10 pence and sometimes more. Ceylons met more demand at dearer rates. No Assams were offered.</p>
<p>Landed packages totalled 3,650 with 1,600 offshore.</p>
<p>Offshore met good demand at fully firm to dearer rates.</p>
<p>The highest price paid for a landed tea was 178 pence for a Burundi PD.</p>
</text>
